<section id="tiers">
<h2>8 · Three-tier policy</h2>
<p>Each application goes to the action with the highest expected value: approve, decline, or manual review (at {{ m.economics.review.cost_per_case | num }} CU per case, a reviewer is assumed to decline
{{ m.economics.review.bad_catch_rate | pct(0) }} of bad applicants and {{ m.economics.review.good_decline_rate | pct(0) }} of good ones). Review only pays near the break-even and for larger loans; when demand exceeds
capacity ({{ m.economics.review.capacity_share | pct(0) }} of each month's applications) the most valuable reviews are kept within each month's cap: {{ m.three_tier.capacity_by_month['202001'] | num }} / {{ m.three_tier.capacity_by_month['202002'] | num }} / {{ m.three_tier.capacity_by_month['202003'] | num }} in January / February / March 2020. No month exceeds its cap. Uncapped demand would be {{ m.three_tier.uncapped_review_per_month | num }} reviews a month.
Volumes are booked-loan volumes; the real queue is set on through-the-door volume, which is larger by the share the lender rejects today.</p>
